# smelting.fk: iron ore and coal into plates, the plates into a provider chest. Plot 26x26, on an
# iron patch (the drills need ore under them). Shows: MinerRow, rot 2, a row (SmelterRow) and the
# `row-cell` advice that writes the Stack of library cells replacing it.
# Run:  fk check smelting.fk    fk rates smelting.fk
# Expect: `could-pair net fuel and ore_` (shared-belt.fk pairs them); `advice row-cell smelt: ...
# Stack<cell=StoneFurnaceCell, n=8, ...>`; 120 plates/min, the furnaces at 80% (ore short).
ore   = MinerRow<n=4, resource=iron-ore>   @(16, 9, rot 2)
coal  = MinerRow<n=2, resource=coal>       @(21, 9, rot 2)
smelt = SmelterRow<n=8, recipe=iron-plate> @(10, 12)
box   = Chest<provider, limit=4>           @(4, 22)

net ore_:   ore -> smelt
net fuel:   coal -> smelt
net plates: smelt -> box
